{# The logo rides with the message rather than being linked or inlined as a
   data: URI: Gmail and Outlook both refuse data: URIs in an image, which is
   what made this logo render broken in a subscriber's inbox. `email.image()`
   attaches the file and hands back the cid: that points at it.

   The same partial heads the confirmation pages, which are served rather than
   sent and have no `email` to attach to; there the logo comes from the site. #}
{% set brand_logo = email is defined ? email.image('@email_assets/brand-logo.png') : '/revue-de-presse.png' %}
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
  <tr>
    <td style="padding-right:12px;vertical-align:middle">
      <img src="{{ brand_logo }}" width="58" height="58" alt="Revue de presse" style="display:block;border:0">
    </td>
    <td style="vertical-align:middle">
      <h1 style="margin:0">Revue de presse</h1>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
